{"name":"Godzilla","hex":"#3c4d03","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Godzilla","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A fictional Japanese monster (kaiju) from a series of science-fiction films."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Anything that is an extremely large or dramatic example of its type."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Godzilla"}],"entries":[{"title":"Godzilla","blocks":[{"text":"Godzilla is a fictional giant monster, or daikaijū, that first appeared in the 1954 film of the same name, directed by Ishirō Honda. The character has since become an international pop culture icon, appearing in various media: 33 Japanese films by Toho, five American films, and numerous video games, novels, comic books, and television shows. Godzilla has been dubbed the King of the Monsters, an epithet first used in Godzilla, King of the Monsters! (1956), the American localization of the 1954 film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Godzilla_%281954%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Godzilla_%281954%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godzilla","wikidata":"Q6567"},{"title":"Godzilla (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Godzilla  is a Japanese kaiju multimedia franchise centering on the titular character, a prehistoric reptilian monster awakened and powered by nuclear radiation. The films series are recognized by the Guinness World Records as the \"longest continuously running film series\", having been in ongoing production since 1954, with several hiatuses of varying lengths. There are 38 Godzilla films: 33 Japanese films produced and distributed by Toho Co., Ltd., and five American films; one by TriStar Pictures and four films by Legendary Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Godzilla_English_Logo.png/330px-Godzilla_English_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Godzilla_(franchise)","wikidata":"Q28859760"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png/500px-Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png/1280px-Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png/500px-Godzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_%281956%29_Atomic_ray.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Godzilla using its atomic breath, as shown in Godzilla (1954)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGodzilla_King_of_the_Monsters_(1956)_Atomic_ray.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Godzilla_%281954%29_Teiz%C3%B4_Toshimitsu.jpg/500px-Godzilla_%281954%29_Teiz%C3%B4_Toshimitsu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Godzilla_%281954%29_Teiz%C3%B4_Toshimitsu.jpg/500px-Godzilla_%281954%29_Teiz%C3%B4_Toshimitsu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Teizō Toshimitsu sculpting a prototype for Godzilla's design","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGodzilla_(1954)_Teiz%C3%B4_Toshimitsu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Godzilla_Raids_Again_%281955%29_Behind_the_scenes.gif/500px-Godzilla_Raids_Again_%281955%29_Behind_the_scenes.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Go